---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const d='/equipment/12-05/',y='https://web-material3.yokogawa.com/2/32993/files/BU80C01D01-01E%20CSU-W1.pdf',n='https://www.microscope.healthcare.nikon.com/products/inverted-microscopes/eclipse-ti-series',b='https://www.microscope.healthcare.nikon.com/bioimaging-centers/nic-and-cofe/university-of-basel-dbm';
---
<Layout pageTitle="CSU-W1 / Nikon Ti-E geometry and offline grid" description="Inspect the static CSU-W1 and Nikon Ti-E reference, then work through an offline fixed calibration-grid stack." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment" id="w1"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/12-05/">← Equipment 12-05</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#w1-evidence">References and checks</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">12-05 / STATIC INSTRUMENT · SEPARATE OFFLINE DATA</p><h2>Reassemble a shifted grid stack</h2><p class="eq-lede">Explore a de-energized CSU-W1 with Nikon Eclipse Ti-E. Then pick a card on the separate stand to compare fixed synthetic planes before and after translating them into the same frame.</p></header>
<div class="w-cols"><section><h3>Exterior and offline card stand</h3><canvas id="w1-model" aria-label="Orbitable static microscope, CSU-W1, and independent three-card stand"></canvas><p id="w1-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="w1-front">Reset overview</button><button id="w1-module">Scanner and adapter</button><button id="w1-cards">Card stand close-up</button></section>
<section><h3>Fixed synthetic dot-grid planes</h3><div class="w-select"><label>Plane<select id="w1-plane"><option value="lower">Lower · 0 µm</option><option value="middle">Middle · 8 µm</option><option value="upper">Upper · 16 µm</option></select></label><label>View<select id="w1-expression"><option value="raw">Original offsets</option><option value="registered">Registered alignment</option></select></label></div><div class="w-grid"><canvas id="w1-grid" width="64" height="64" role="img" aria-label="Selected synthetic grid"></canvas><div>32 µm</div></div><p id="w1-readout" role="status"></p><button id="w1-export">Download this plane as JSON</button><p><a href={d+'example-grid.json'}>Example: registered middle plane</a>. The image row axis points down. The 16-pixel bar and mark spacing are 32 µm. Use the dropdowns without WebGL.</p></section></div>
<section id="w1-evidence"><h3>Source views and geometric scope</h3><div class="w-cols">
<figure><img src={d+'station.webp'} alt="Original render of the white inverse microscope and scanner beside a separate colored card stand"/><figcaption>Original exterior render. The <a href={n}>Nikon Ti-series vendor photo</a> supports the inverted stand silhouette; <a href={b}>Nikon's Basel facility page</a> confirms real Ti-E and CSU-W1 pairings, not an identical local installation.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src={d+'module.webp'} alt="Original render of the ivory and charcoal CSU-W1 and capped interface"/><figcaption>Original three-quarter view. <a href={y+'#page=1'}>Yokogawa cover photograph</a> shows the T1 enclosure, angled panel and exterior caps; <a href={y+'#page=6'}>dimensioned T1 views (printed pp. 9–10)</a> and the <a href={y+'#page=7'}>general specifications</a> anchor the older horizontal T1 version.</figcaption></figure>
</div>
<table><thead><tr><th>Quantity</th><th>Value</th><th>Evidence / scope</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>CSU-W1 horizontal T1 assembly envelope</td><td>480 × 327 × 252 mm (W × D × H)</td><td>Yokogawa legacy brochure. Export checked to 2.5 mm; covers mock adapter and feet. Case profile, small features and interfaces inferred.</td></tr><tr><td>Stand, camera cap and mount</td><td>Nominal / inferred</td><td>Ti-series profile only. No actual camera, internal disk or powered components modeled.</td></tr><tr><td>Offline raster and plane positions</td><td>64 × 64 px, 2 µm/px; 0, 8, 16 µm</td><td>Authored metric labels, not optical calibration or equipment travel.</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3>Independent analytical checks</h3><p>Nine equal symmetric marks have a mean center at (32, 32) pixels. Raw middle adds (+4, −3) pixels; registration subtracts that same declared offset exactly using integer coordinate translation. No interpolation or optical model is implemented.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual / tolerance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Lower to raw middle centroid</td><td>(64, 64) → (72, 58) µm</td><td>Exact within 10⁻¹⁰ µm</td></tr><tr><td>Registered upper and lower rasters</td><td>All 4,096 values match</td><td>4,096 match, exact</td></tr><tr><td>Adjacent mark centers</td><td>32 µm</td><td>32 µm, exact</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Offline raster reading only. The register's moving-point exposure/motion-blur test is not implemented. No acquisition, specimen, or hardware interaction is simulated.</p><p><a href={d+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={d+'csu-w1-tie.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={d+'fixed-grid.mjs'}>Offline readout and JSON schema</a> · <a href={d+'vr.json'}>VR interaction IDs and bounds</a>. Headset performance not verified.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/12-05/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>
#w1 .w-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.25fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#w1 section{margin:1rem 0;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);min-width:0}
#w1 :is(button,select){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.4rem;margin:.2rem .2rem .2rem 0;max-width:100%}#w1 button{cursor:pointer}
#w1 :is(button,select):focus-visible{outline:2px solid #b28d5e}
#w1 .w-select{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.6rem}#w1 label{display:grid;margin:.3rem 0}#w1-model{display:block;width:100%;height:340px;touch-action:none}
#w1 .w-grid{position:relative;width:min(100%,290px);margin:.35rem auto}.w-grid div{position:absolute;right:7%;bottom:6%;width:25%;color:#eee6dc;border-bottom:3px solid;text-align:center;font:11px system-ui;pointer-events:none}
#w1-grid{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated}
#w1 figure{margin:.5rem 0}#w1 figure img{width:100%}
#w1 table{width:100%;font-size:.94rem;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left}#w1 td,#w1 th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}
@media(max-width:850px){#w1 .w-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#w1-model{height:266px}#w1 .w-grid{width:min(80%,275px)}}
</style>
